      "path": "src/ui/backup/RestoreFlow.tsx",
      "content": "This forwards arbitrary rejection text to console.error without sanitization (`logFailure` writes the detail unchanged). An exception message can contain backup record values—for example, a JSON parsing SyntaxError can quote the input—and `Error.stack` normally repeats that message. Stringifying non-Error rejections can likewise expose journal contents. This violates the explicit no-journal-contents logging requirement. Log a fixed failure message and allowlisted diagnostic metadata instead of raw exception text, or use a sanitization contract that also covers stacks. Add a regression test with sensitive content in an Error and a string rejection.",
